#X text 215 80 || Versions <5.0;
#X text 215 105 The BCM283x SoC supports 2 hardware PWM channels. By
default \, the channels are mapped as follows:;
#X text 215 145 • PWM0 = GPIO12/GPIO18;
#X text 215 170 • PWM1 = GPIO13/GPIO19;
#X text 215 195 Consult the official documentation on how to enable
and configure these.;
#X text 215 235 Note: the Raspberry Pi?s analog audio output uses both
PWM channels. Playing audio and simultaneously accessing a PWM channel
may cause issues.;
#X text 215 290 ~;
#X text 215 315 || Raspberry Pi 5 and later;
#X text 215 340 The Raspberry Pi 5 support 4 hardware PWM channels.
By default \, the channels are mapped as follows:;
#X text 215 380 • PWM0 = GPIO12;
#X text 215 405 • PWM1 = GPIO13;
#X text 215 430 • PWM2 = GPIO18;
#X text 215 455 • PWM3 = GPIO19;
#X text 215 480 Consult the official documentation on how to enable
and configure these.;
#X text 215 520 ~;
#X text 215 545 Some of the GPIO pins capable of supporting hardware
PWM can also be configured for use with other peripherals. Be careful
not to enable two peripherals on the same pin at the same time.;
